Apple is preparing what appear to be giant <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-duo/">iPhone Duo</a> displays outside its Fifth Avenue store in New York ahead of the device's launch on Friday, October 23.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2025/03/Apple-Fifth-Avenue-Hero.jpeg" alt="" width="2880" height="1612" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-995482" /><br/>
<a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/photos/">Photos</a> from users on X show the structures on the plaza beside the glass cube. Their designs are hidden by wrapping and black covers, so it remains unclear exactly how Apple will present the device.<br/>
<br/>
<div class="center-wrap"><blockquote class="twitter-tweet"><a href="https://twitter.com/LChenlz/status/2112997046806307287">October 21, 2026</a></blockquote><script async src="https://platform.twitter.com/widgets.js" charset="utf-8"></script></div><br/>
<br/>
The outdoor installations accompany a substantial retail push inside the store. According to <em>Bloomberg</em>'s <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/mark-gurman/">Mark Gurman</a>, Apple plans to allocate <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/11/iphone-duo-retail-showcase/">more than 150 iPhone Duo units</a> to demonstrations and displays at Fifth Avenue. Typical non-flagship locations are expected to receive around 20 each.<br/>
<br/>
Gurman also described new ways to demonstrate the foldable design, including a fixture that shows the device opening and closing. A separate <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/magsafe/">MagSafe</a> stand will hold an unfolded &zwnj;iPhone Duo&zwnj; beside two conventional iPhones for comparison.<br/>
<br/>
Fifth Avenue's launch decorations have changed twice in just over a month. For September's <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-18-pro/">iPhone 18 Pro</a> release, Apple <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/17/john-ternus-teases-iphone-18-pro-launch/">added color to the cube</a> to reflect the new Burgundy and Glacier finishes.<br/>
<br/>
The &zwnj;iPhone Duo&zwnj; goes on sale on Friday, October 23. Apple has <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/21/apple-stores-limited-iphone-duo-for-walk-in/">confirmed limited walk-in availability</a> in the United States and several other markets, warning that launch-day inventory is expected to sell out quickly. Stores in mainland China, France, Japan, and several other markets will require customers to reserve a pickup time through Apple's online store.<br/>
